  "name": "delivery-event-lane-gaps",
  "description": "Change C6, opt-in: with reportEventLaneGaps, events evicted from the pending queue or the retry queue and batches rejected for good are reported as collector_event_upload gaps when the cumulative count crosses a power of two. A gap event is an ordinary event, so queueing it can evict another. The gap event queued while the rejected batch was in flight waits for the next pass: a pass drains only the events queued when it reached them (Dart 0.11.1). Delivery's own collector_request reports (Dart 0.11.1) are events like any other: they join batches and take request ids, so a request a step answers may be a batch of reports, and step notes describe the state without them.",
